features/structs (lacks) / a record lacking a field it DECLARES / the declaration refuses, naming the field
features/structs (lacks) / a record lacking one field twice / the declaration refuses — one reason per field
features/structs (lacks) / an enum wearing `@lacks` / the declaration refuses — only a record has fields to lack
features/structs (lacks) / two fields lacked, each for its own reason / each read hears its own
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed enum, built outside its module / a bare variant refuses though the type is never imported
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed enum, built outside its module / a variant named through the type refuses, carrying or not
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed enum, built outside its module / a variant with a payload refuses
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed name over text, at every other seat a literal reaches / an alias of the name, and a name over it
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed name over text, at every other seat a literal reaches / an annotation's argument, filled across the crossing
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed name over text, at every other seat a literal reaches / the fallback of `??`
features/structs (sealed) / a sealed name over text, built outside its module / `Name(value)` does not convert into it
features/structs (sealed) / generated code / a template that lands in another module does not build its own package's sealed type
features/structs (sealed) / the refusal, rendered / a conversion outside the module
features/sublang — a block is its grammar's actions / the word / a file that does not import the word reads `sql {` as the language always did — a name, then a block it cannot parse
features/sublang — adversarial / two imports of one word / the second import of a word another package already binds refuses at the use, naming the holder
features/tasks / a caught await / a variant arm is refused — a `Cancelled` has none to name
features/tasks.channel / a spawned reader the block never lets end / no `close()` before the block ends is refused by name
features/tasks.channel / what it answers / a capacity that is no `int` is refused by name
# The cases that read a lone program's IR (ir_of), pinned when ir_of moved onto the program layer. Each
# asserts an INSTRUCTION the layer's IR lacks or orders otherwise, never a name: a `const` seat lowered as
# one body where the old path split a unit per settled value; a deferred call through a closure box; a
# scheduler test or shield the layer leaves out; a map write's probe, a loop's end cell, a chain's or a
# `chars()` walk's single loop; a borrow, a release or a consumed mark its memory pass places otherwise;
# a spawned lone program it does not make. The same rule: the list only shrinks.
compiler/lower — the test after a call /  / a compiler unit's call is tested — no `wanted` name to judge it by
compiler/lower — the test after a call /  / a task's cold exit answers an EMPTY cell, never a null a joiner reads
compiler/lower — a checked `while` back-edge /  / a top-level park links the scheduler for a top-level `while`
compiler/cancel_reach — what links a scheduler /  / a `defer` beside a call through a value, nothing spawned: the cold exit carries no shield
features/fns / an extern seat's machine WIDTH / the widths leave pointer seats alone
features/loops / the loop in the IR, as `avra ir` prints it / a for reads its end once — a count cell stepped as the turn begins, the name's cell per turn
a parameter's consumed mark, read off ir_of's own lowering / a seat stored whole on every path to the answer / the body's own lowered marks say so — a one-shot workspace must still ask R3 at lowering
a comprehension lowers as one nest of walks / an indexed head, a filter, a list head and a range head reading earlier binders / each head opens inside the one before it, each filter guards the rest
a method chain folds into one pipeline / a filter, a map, then a sum / one loop, no list, the accumulator carried across turns
a method chain folds into one pipeline / a filter then a terminal / one loop, no list, the verdict ended on its first hit
a method chain folds into one pipeline / a filter then a map / one loop, both fn boxes read before it, the element pushed once
features/mutation — a `state` local is a Cell / an unannotated `state` local / its slot and its loads wear `Cell<R>`
features/mutation — a `state` local is a Cell / an annotated `state` local / its slot and its loads wear `Cell<R>`
compiler/lower — a checked `while` back-edge /  / an `@unbroken` fn's own `while` carries no check
# "The subset today" (compiler/subset): refusals the old path speaks that the program layer does not, pinned
# when the spec moved onto it — each is a form the layer accepts or leaves unjudged.
compiler/subset — syntax the grammar lacks / syntax the grammar lacks / `.length` on a range is refused beside range scans that compile
compiler/subset — syntax the grammar lacks / syntax the grammar lacks / `fail` inside a `catch` block is refused
compiler/subset — syntax the grammar lacks / syntax the grammar lacks / a bare generic fn as a value is refused in words
compiler/subset — syntax the grammar lacks / syntax the grammar lacks / an empty block as a match arm is an empty map
compiler/subset — wants the typer does not carry yet / wants the typer does not carry yet / a bound method as a value is read as a property
# component_home: a component word nobody imported is told the module that exports it — the layer's refusal offers
# no such remedy and reads no file of the other package (the two read-bound cases pass at zero reads).
component_home — one lookup's reads do not grow with the lookups / twelve modules each exporting a component / a word nobody imported is told the module that exports it
# compiler/workspace (adversarial): the module system under attack, asked of held packages — what the layer
# says otherwise: an import clash it leaves unsaid, a re-export cycle, a duplicate said under another kind.
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / a field default is a body of its module / a default reading its file's top-level binding refuses in ITS file, not the literal's
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / a type's methods are one namespace across its module's files / the same method in two files of one module clashes at the LATER file, only
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / names against names / an import shadowed by a local declaration refuses
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / names against names / the same name from two modules refuses
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / private names two files declare / a kept-apart type named in a third file's signature is refused as kept apart
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / private names two files declare / an import of a name this file keeps apart refuses
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / re-exports / a module that declares a name twice is refused once — the re-exports and imports meeting it stay silent
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / re-exports / a re-export claims its name against a sibling's private declaration
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / re-exports / a re-export from a package that already uses this one is refused as a cycle
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / re-exports / a re-export of an item its module does not export refuses as not exported
compiler/workspace (adversarial) / re-exports / an importer's own declaration of a re-exported name refuses
# compiler/packages, asked of held packages:
compiler/packages / a package sees only what its manifest declares / a transitive dependency is invisible, and the fix writes the line
# compiler/workspace, asked of held packages: an unread module's names staying silent beside its parse error,
# a nested module's symbol, and two package-graph refusals the layer words otherwise or leaves unsaid.
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / a failed use's names answer to the use alone — a type read and a call both stay silent
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / a local declaration of a refused name still answers its reads
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / a refused item named as an impl's trait, a `dyn` and a bound stays silent beside its use
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / an aliased item of an unread module — the alias's reads are silent too
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / an impl's trait, a `dyn` and a bound refused in a module with an unread file point at it
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / an item its module's unread file would have declared — the parse error named, the reads silent
compiler/workspace / a failed use speaks / an item the unread module never named is refused with the parse error beside it
compiler/workspace / typed across ws_files — the table is one / a nested module's fn lowers under its qualified symbol
the prelude / the floor / a prelude that declares a dependency is refused
the toolchain's std packages / a manifest row for a std package / a dependency's own row disagreeing with the pin is two directories
# compiler/warm, asked of the layer over one store: the warm report IS the cold one in all 13 cases; this case's
# refusal is not in the words the spec names ("the body answers").
compiler/warm — a report read over a store is the report of an empty one /  / a literal const's type moved refuses its unchanged reader
# decl grain, asked of the layer as main's share of an edit (what its judging works out past a bystander's):
#   a comment in / a new body for `one`: main asks item_misses and item_receivers again (1-2 answers);
#   a declaration added / `two` renamed: main is TYPED again (typed_fn, module_declares, record_signature,
#   alias_target x3, named_shape, trait_method_signature) — it reads the module's declarations, not the names it uses;
#   a deprecated fn's new note: main asks again, and its build says no deprecation warning at all.
compiler/workspace — a use reads the declaration, never its file / a caller of a deprecated fn in another file / a new note moves the frontier, and the warning says it
compiler/workspace — a use reads the declaration, never its file / the other file edited where the caller cannot see / a comment above and inside `one` keeps every query of main's, answering alike
compiler/workspace — a use reads the declaration, never its file / the other file edited where the caller cannot see / a new body for `one` keeps them
compiler/workspace — a use reads the declaration, never its file / the other file's declarations added or renamed where the caller does not read / `two`, which the caller never names, renamed keeps them
